1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,840
Here are three equations
that look almost the same.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,296
x squared minus six x, plus five.

3
00:00:06,296 --> 00:00:07,196
Plus nine.

4
00:00:07,179 --> 00:00:08,265
Plus thirteen.

5
00:00:08,665 --> 00:00:10,878
One has two different real roots.

6
00:00:10,878 --> 00:00:12,992
One has a single repeated root.

7
00:00:12,992 --> 00:00:15,273
And one has no real root at all.

8
00:00:15,723 --> 00:00:18,454
Aarav was stuck on these
at his desk last night.

9
00:00:18,804 --> 00:00:22,084
Can you tell which is which,
without solving a single one?

10
00:00:22,584 --> 00:00:23,484
You can.

11
00:00:23,311 --> 00:00:26,270
One small number decides
it, before you solve.

12
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:28,207
It is called the discriminant.

13
00:00:28,857 --> 00:00:32,412
Recall the quadratic formula
from the last episode.

14
00:00:32,762 --> 00:00:35,173
Minus b over two a is just a number.

15
00:00:35,173 --> 00:00:38,822
Only the part under the root
can change the kind of answer.

16
00:00:39,222 --> 00:00:43,260
That part, b squared minus four
a c, is called the discriminant.

17
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:44,979
We write it as capital D.

18
00:00:45,379 --> 00:00:49,888
Its job is to discriminate, which means
to tell apart, the kinds of roots.

19
00:00:50,538 --> 00:00:52,751
Watch D and the curve together.

20
00:00:52,751 --> 00:00:57,515
y equals x squared minus six x plus
c, with c counting up from five.

21
00:00:57,915 --> 00:01:01,920
At c equals five, D is thirty
six minus twenty, sixteen.

22
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:02,820
Positive.

23
00:01:02,699 --> 00:01:06,079
The curve cuts the axis
twice, at one and five.

24
00:01:06,479 --> 00:01:10,649
As c grows, D shrinks, and the two
roots slide towards each other.

25
00:01:11,049 --> 00:01:13,376
At c equals nine, D hits zero.

26
00:01:13,376 --> 00:01:16,225
The curve just touches the axis at three.

27
00:01:16,225 --> 00:01:18,018
The two roots are equal.

28
00:01:18,418 --> 00:01:21,143
Push c past nine, and D turns negative.

29
00:01:21,143 --> 00:01:23,163
The curve lifts off the axis.

30
00:01:23,563 --> 00:01:28,115
On the Argand plane, the roots
split into a pair, one up, one down.

31
00:01:28,115 --> 00:01:32,523
At c equals thirteen, D is minus
sixteen, and the roots are three plus

32
00:01:32,523 --> 00:01:33,762
and minus two i.

33
00:01:34,412 --> 00:01:35,330
Quick one.

34
00:01:35,330 --> 00:01:40,284
For x squared plus two x plus five,
is D positive, zero or negative?

35
00:01:40,284 --> 00:01:41,583
Pause and think.

36
00:01:44,783 --> 00:01:45,683
Negative!

37
00:01:45,604 --> 00:01:48,489
D is four minus twenty, minus sixteen.

38
00:01:48,489 --> 00:01:52,725
So the roots are complex:
minus one plus and minus two i.

39
00:01:53,375 --> 00:01:56,008
Why does the sign of D decide everything?

40
00:01:56,008 --> 00:01:57,760
Look at the formula again.

41
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,060
Step one.

42
00:01:59,049 --> 00:02:04,046
The roots are minus b over two a,
plus or minus root D over two a.

43
00:02:04,796 --> 00:02:05,696
Step two.

44
00:02:05,678 --> 00:02:09,504
If D is positive, root D
is a positive real number.

45
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:12,707
Plus and minus give two
different real roots.

46
00:02:13,457 --> 00:02:14,420
Step three.

47
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:16,806
If D is zero, root D is zero.

48
00:02:16,806 --> 00:02:21,287
Plus and minus give the same
root, minus b over two a, twice.

49
00:02:22,037 --> 00:02:22,958
Step four.

50
00:02:22,958 --> 00:02:26,738
If D is negative, root D
is i times a real number.

51
00:02:26,738 --> 00:02:29,671
The roots are complex, a conjugate pair.

52
00:02:30,421 --> 00:02:34,060
So the sign of D tells you the
kind of roots, with no solving.

53
00:02:34,710 --> 00:02:37,949
One more split, when a,
b and c are rational.

54
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:39,715
Take D greater than zero.

55
00:02:40,115 --> 00:02:44,678
If D is a perfect square, its root
is a whole number, and the roots are

56
00:02:44,678 --> 00:02:45,578
rational.

57
00:02:45,407 --> 00:02:48,771
For x squared minus six x
plus five, D is sixteen.

58
00:02:48,771 --> 00:02:50,650
The roots are one and five.

59
00:02:51,050 --> 00:02:54,967
If not, the root stays a surd,
and the roots are irrational.

60
00:02:54,967 --> 00:02:58,218
For x squared minus six
x plus seven, D is eight.

61
00:02:58,218 --> 00:03:01,900
The roots are three plus root
two and three minus root two.

62
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,400
Your turn.

63
00:03:03,386 --> 00:03:05,697
x squared minus four x plus one.

64
00:03:05,697 --> 00:03:07,825
Rational roots, or irrational?

65
00:03:07,825 --> 00:03:09,128
Pause and decide.

66
00:03:12,328 --> 00:03:13,228
Irrational!

67
00:03:13,176 --> 00:03:16,871
D is sixteen minus four,
twelve, not a perfect square.

68
00:03:16,871 --> 00:03:19,817
The roots are two plus
and minus root three.

69
00:03:20,467 --> 00:03:21,444
Remember this.

70
00:03:21,444 --> 00:03:23,189
Check the sign of D first.

71
00:03:23,189 --> 00:03:26,158
It tells you the kind of
roots before you solve.

72
00:03:26,858 --> 00:03:28,593
Now, one worked example.

73
00:03:28,943 --> 00:03:34,677
Find k, so that x squared minus k x
plus nine equals zero has equal roots.

74
00:03:35,177 --> 00:03:36,077
Step one.

75
00:03:36,002 --> 00:03:39,345
Here a is one, b is
minus k, and c is nine.

76
00:03:40,095 --> 00:03:40,995
Step two.

77
00:03:40,989 --> 00:03:43,465
D is k squared minus thirty six.

78
00:03:44,215 --> 00:03:45,213
Step three.

79
00:03:45,213 --> 00:03:47,608
Equal roots means D equals zero.

80
00:03:47,608 --> 00:03:49,733
So k squared is thirty six.

81
00:03:50,483 --> 00:03:51,383
Step four.

82
00:03:51,331 --> 00:03:53,505
k is six, or k is minus six.

83
00:03:54,255 --> 00:03:58,254
Check: with k equal to six,
it is x minus three, squared.

84
00:03:58,254 --> 00:03:59,748
Both roots are three.

85
00:04:00,398 --> 00:04:01,864
Now, the exam trap.

86
00:04:02,214 --> 00:04:06,505
The equation x squared minus two
k x plus four has real roots.

87
00:04:06,505 --> 00:04:11,326
Many students write D greater than
zero, and get k greater than two, or

88
00:04:11,326 --> 00:04:12,874
less than minus two.

89
00:04:13,274 --> 00:04:15,410
But equal roots are real too.

90
00:04:15,410 --> 00:04:19,049
Real roots means D is greater
than or equal to zero.

91
00:04:19,049 --> 00:04:22,325
So k is at least two,
or at most minus two.

92
00:04:22,975 --> 00:04:24,422
Where is this asked?

93
00:04:24,422 --> 00:04:29,037
In JEE Main, where a condition on the
roots becomes a condition on D, as

94
00:04:29,037 --> 00:04:30,932
in August twenty twenty one.

95
00:04:30,932 --> 00:04:35,459
You met D in Class ten, but it is
not in the current Class eleven NCERT

96
00:04:35,459 --> 00:04:36,359
text.

97
00:04:36,603 --> 00:04:37,900
Exam level now.

98
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:43,000
For how many integer values of k does
this equation have no real roots?

99
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,352
Pause and solve.

100
00:04:49,752 --> 00:04:50,932
The answer is B.

101
00:04:50,932 --> 00:04:51,832
Four.

102
00:04:51,944 --> 00:04:55,111
No real roots means D is less than zero.

103
00:04:55,111 --> 00:04:58,867
D is four k squared minus
four times k plus six.

104
00:04:59,367 --> 00:05:00,629
Divide by four.

105
00:05:00,629 --> 00:05:03,997
k squared minus k minus
six is less than zero.

106
00:05:03,997 --> 00:05:07,088
That is k minus three, times k plus two.

107
00:05:07,588 --> 00:05:12,304
A product is negative only when its
factors have opposite signs: k between

108
00:05:12,304 --> 00:05:13,822
minus two and three.

109
00:05:13,822 --> 00:05:17,173
The integers are minus
one, zero, one and two.

110
00:05:17,173 --> 00:05:18,161
Four values.

111
00:05:18,761 --> 00:05:20,225
Here is your recap.

112
00:05:20,225 --> 00:05:21,730
Screenshot this card.

113
00:05:24,930 --> 00:05:27,766
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

114
00:05:28,166 --> 00:05:29,066
One.

115
00:05:28,671 --> 00:05:31,945
Find D for two x squared
plus three x plus four.

116
00:05:31,945 --> 00:05:34,190
What kind of roots does it have?

117
00:05:35,090 --> 00:05:35,990
Two.

118
00:05:35,629 --> 00:05:38,954
Why does D equal to zero
give two equal roots?

119
00:05:39,854 --> 00:05:40,754
Three.

120
00:05:40,525 --> 00:05:45,871
For which values of k does x squared
plus k x plus four have equal roots?

121
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:51,687
Next time: add the two roots, multiply
them, and get two simple numbers

122
00:05:51,687 --> 00:05:54,227
from a, b and c, without solving.
